  "derivation": {
   "source_inclusion": "The canonical unit snub cube lies in beta times the canonical unit truncated cuboctahedron in the identity frame, beta=2R/(1+2sqrt2), where R=alpha\u00b2/sqrt(2+2alpha\u00b2) and alpha\u00b3=alpha\u00b2+alpha+1. The square-face radii agree. With y=1/alpha, the snub cube absolute coordinate set is R*{1,y,y\u00b2}; all pair and triple signed supports lie strictly inside the remaining TCO walls.",
   "initial_whole_owner_lift": "Multiply every complete source center by beta and replace each beta-scaled TCO by the enclosed canonical SNC in the same exact source quaternion.",
   "source_frames": "All source quaternions are retained exactly.",
